sqlite3 app.db "PRAGMA busy_timeout;"
```

**Fallback Pattern (if timeout insufficient):**
```javascript
function queryWithRetry(sql, retries = 3) {
  for (let i = 0; i < retries; i++) {
    try {
      return db.query(sql).all();
    } catch (err) {
      if (err.code !== 'SQLITE_BUSY') throw err;
      Bun.sleep(100 * (i + 1)); // Exponential backoff
    }
  }
  throw new Error('Max retries exceeded');
}
```

The timeout approach leverages SQLite engine's native contention resolution while maintaining your single-user/local-first constraints. No architectural changes required.

